  "designer": "AI agent (Claude) proposed adding Hurricane's screening pool to its classifier as non-superconducting background compounds, at three weights, after Konno et al. (2021), and the database-swap check",
  "selection": "5-fold GroupKFold by parent compound on 2,123 3DSC entries, the same folds and seeds as rounds 1 and 2; the background in 5 folds by chemical system, fold k paired with 3DSC fold k; leave-one-family-out and anchors reported, never used to choose",
  "rule": "release the design with the fewest false alarms among those that, against Hurricane 2.0 on the same folds, raise at most 0.5 times as many false alarms on the held-out background compounds that Radar sends to Hurricane and fewer in at least 4 of 5 folds, are not more than 0.3 K worse on measured Tc and 0.5 K worse on the superconducting entries, have a Brier score at most 0.01 worse, and whose chance drops by at most 0.05 more than Hurricane 2.0's when 3DSC compounds are described with JARVIS structures instead of their own",
  "caveat": "The background compounds have no superconductivity record, which is not a measurement of zero: most were probably never tested and a few may superconduct. Counting them as non-superconducting makes Hurricane more cautious about chemistry unlike its training data, including a family that nobody has found yet.",
